    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "β-hemoglobinpathies, such as sickle cell disease (SCD) and β-thalassemia, are blood disorders that directly affect millions of people around the world.  The only curative treatment for these blood disorders is by allogeneic-hematopoietic stem cell transplant (allo-HSCT), which faces a shortage of immunologically matched donors and other severe limitations1, 2.   With the lack of effective curative therapies, it is postulated that autologous HSCT of gene edited hematopoietic stem/progenitor cells (HSPCs) would be a potential cure for patients afflicted with either of the β-hemoglobinpathies.  The goal of this project was to create an alternative curative approach for these diseases that uses genome correction to directly correct the HBB gene through insertion of a wild-type β-globin cDNA to an endogenous start codon in the patient’s own HSPCs.  The Porteus lab has designed and optimized an HBB-specific CRISPR/Cas9 ribonucleic (RNP)3 –based platform, in which we achieved homologous recombination (HR)-mediated targeting rates of ~25%-30% in human CD34+ HSPCs shown with fluorescence-activated cell sorting (FACS) analysis.  Our CRISPR/Cas9 complexed with chemically modified sgRNAs RNP platform using rAAV6 donor transduction can achieve therapeutically relevant frequencies of HR-mediated gene correction in an HSPC population. Further, we show that we can effectively enrich a targeted tNGFR+, a non-immunogenic, truncated nerve growth receptor (tNGFR)4, HSPC population to >85% HR-mediated cells through micro-magnetic bead enrichment by Day 3 post-electroporation.  Notably, these genomically edited HSPCs are capable of multi-lineage differentiation and have progenitor potential further demonstrating how an optimized CRISPR/Cas9 nuclease platform in combination with rAAV6 can become an ideal candidate for therapeutic application.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
